  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1133 PM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nThe weak ridge overhead breaks down Tuesday as a trough moves \nsoutheast across the northern and central Rockies and Great Plains. \nHigh temperatures warm a touch more. Upper level ridging over the \nGreat Basin and troughing over the Great Plains Wednesday helps \nsends a backdoor front through eastern NM during the morning hours \nresulting in some breezy north winds. The GFS is on the higher end \nwith north wind gusts up to 40 mph due to slightly stronger 700 mb \nwinds of 25 to 30 kts because of the trough sliding further west \ncompared to the other mid range guidance. The upper ridge slides \neast over the state Wednesday night into Thursday sliding east of \nthe state late Friday. This will allow the tranquil November weather \nto continue! High to mid level clouds move in from the west Friday \nnight into Saturday as an upper low moves into southern CA. Showers \ncould impact west central, southwest and south central NM as early \nas Saturday afternoon as the upper low moves across southern CA and \nAZ and northwest Mexico. High temperatures this week will be near to \nas much as 10 degrees above average for mid November. Slight cooling \nacross eastern NM Wednesday due to the backdoor front. Low temperatures\nwill be 5 to 12 degrees above average for mid November.",
